  <article class="almanac-prose">
    <section id="three-clocks" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>04.1 · scheduling vocabulary</span>
        <h2>A timeout, a fuel budget, and a time slice are not synonyms.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="clock-cards">
        <article>
          <div class="clock-glyph clock-wall" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
          <span>wall clock</span><h3>Deadline / timeout</h3>
          <p>Bounds elapsed time for the whole operation. On expiry, current Dekopon increments the engine epoch and the guest traps. A future async host can also cancel the surrounding future.</p>
          <strong>Answers: “has this run taken too long?”</strong>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="clock-glyph clock-fuel" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span>deterministic work</span><h3>Fuel budget</h3>
          <p>Instrumented guest execution consumes units. Exhaustion traps. With Wasmtime async support, an interval can also return <code>Poll::Pending</code> before the total budget is exhausted.</p>
          <strong>Answers: “how much guest work may run?”</strong>
        </article>
        <article>
          <div class="clock-glyph clock-slice" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span>executor fairness</span><h3>Yield interval</h3>
          <p>Temporarily suspends an unfinished guest future so the executor can poll other tasks. Epochs give lower-overhead, timer-like slices; fuel gives deterministic work slices.</p>
          <strong>Answers: “when can another task run?”</strong>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="current-vs-future-strip">
        <div>{{ status("current", "Current") }}<p><strong>Fuel traps at exhaustion.</strong> A deadline thread increments the epoch only at timeout. Calls are synchronous and mutex-serialized, so there is no cooperative time-slicing.</p></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div>{{ status("exploration", "Future host sketch") }}<p><strong>Async host waits return <code>Pending</code>.</strong> Guest compute would also yield periodically, while a total deadline and total work budget still terminate abuse.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

